@761 = ~Entropic Weapon~
@762 = ~Entropic Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 3 rounds / 2 levels
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: special
Saving Throw: none

This spell conjures in the warlord's hands a bubble of wild magic that he shapes into a weapon he knows how to use. The weapon cannot leave his hand for the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped in the same way. This weapon also disrupts everything it hits. It destabilizes the molecules of any armor (natural or not) that it hits and gives a +2 bonus to attack rolls. It causes a metabolic shock where it hits and inflicts 1D8 +3 additional damage. It also disrupts magical energy, and any summoned creature struck is immediately sent back (a save vs. spell prevents banishment, at -3 for demons and -6 for other creatures). Finally each hit of the weapon negates a magical protection of the victim (saving throw at -3 to resist), and leaves some wild magic residue that automatically causes any spell cast to fail in the following round.

Note: Do not create a two-handed sword or a halberd if you are equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, then remove your shield first.~
@76291 = ~Entropic Sword~
@76292 = ~Entropic Katana~
@76293 = ~Entropic Axe~
@76294 = ~Entropic Hammer~
@76295 = ~Entropic Flail~
@76296 = ~Entropic Halberd~
@76297 = ~Entropic Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: special
Saving Throw: none

This spell conjures in the warlord's hands a bubble of wild magic that he shapes into a weapon he knows how to use. The weapon cannot leave his hand for the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped in the same way. This weapon also disrupts everything it hits. It destabilizes the molecules of any armor (natural or not) that it hits and gives a +2 bonus to attack rolls. It causes a metabolic shock where it hits and inflicts 1D8 +3 additional damage. It also disrupts magical energy, and any summoned creature struck is immediately sent back (a save vs. spell prevents banishment, at -3 for demons and -6 for other creatures). Finally each hit of the weapon negates a magical protection of the victim (saving throw at -3 to resist), and leaves some wild magic residue that automatically causes any spell cast to fail in the following round.

Note: Do not create a two-handed sword or a halberd if you are equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, then remove your shield first.~
@76298 = ~Entropic Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell conjures in the recipient's hands a bubble of wild magic that the warlord shapes into a weapon he chose during casting. The weapon cannot leave the hand of the recipient for the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped in the same way. This weapon also disrupts everything it hits. It destabilizes the molecules of any armor (natural or not) that it hits and gives a +2 bonus to attack rolls. It causes a metabolic shock where it hits and inflicts 1D8 +3 additional damage. It also disrupts magical energy, and any summoned creature struck is immediately sent back (a save vs. spell prevents banishment, at -3 for demons and -6 for other creatures). Finally each hit of the weapon negates a magical protection of the victim (saving throw at -3 to resist), and leaves some wild magic residue that automatically causes any spell cast to fail in the following round.

Note: don't create a two-handed sword or a halberd if the recipient is equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, remove the shield first.~
@762981 = ~Entropic Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell conjures in the recipient's hands a bubble of wild magic that the warlord shapes into a weapon he chose during casting. The weapon cannot leave the hand of the recipient for the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped in the same way. This weapon also disrupts everything it hits. It destabilizes the molecules of any armor (natural or not) that it hits and gives a +2 bonus to attack rolls. It causes a metabolic shock where it hits and inflicts 1D8 +3 additional damage. It also disrupts magical energy, and any summoned creature struck is immediately sent back (a save vs. spell prevents banishment, at -3 for demons and -6 for other creatures). Finally each hit of the weapon negates a magical protection of the victim (saving throw at -3 to resist), and leaves some wild magic residue that automatically causes any spell cast to fail in the following round.

All allies within 5 meters of the recipient also benefit from reduced effects of the spell: the same weapon appears in their hands for 2 turns.

Note: don't create a two-handed sword or a halberd if one of the recipients is equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, remove the shield first.~

@763 = ~Wind Armor~
@764 = ~Wind Armor (Invocation)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: special

The warlord developed this spell by refining one of his more remarkable attempts to control the weather:
when the spell is cast, all the winds in the nearby area wrap around the caster and begin to swirl, forming an armor of swirling wind. As long as he is protected by this armor, he is protected from strong winds, disperses clouds and flames (+75% fire resistance), deflects all missiles (+10 to AC) and disrupts other attacks (+2 to AC). In addition, any creature approaching him must make a save vs. breath weapon or will be violently pushed back 10 meters.
This spell can only be used outdoors.~
@7641 = ~Wind Armor (Invocation)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 25 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: special

