Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

When cast, this spell surrounds the recipient with a defensive maelstrom of energy that blocks or deflects many attacks. This gives the recipient a +9 bonus to armor class and an 18% resistance to damage. It also gives the recipient immunity to nonmagical missile-based attacks (though well-thrown axes and spears can still penetrate it).

All allies within 5 meters of the recipient also benefit from reduced effects of the spell:
They get a +6 bonus to AC and 12% resistance for 9 rounds.~

@767 = ~Cloudkill~
@768 = ~Cloudkill (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: 10 meters
Duration: 9 rounds
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: radius 9 meters
Saving Throw: none

The mage creates a concentrated ball of acid in his hands and throws it at the chosen location. It bursts into acrid vapor that fills the area. The vapor quickly thickens, restricting vision and movement (-3 to THAC0, -30% movement speed). Each round, creatures in the cloud suffer 3d6 points of acid damage and must save vs. poison to avoid intoxication. An intoxicated creature loses 2 points of Strength and Dexterity for 1 round and must make another save or suffer severe poisoning: 2 points of damage per second during the current round and 1 point per second during the following round.~
@7681 = ~Cloudkill (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: 10 meters
Duration: 9 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: radius 9 meters
Saving Throw: none

The mage creates a concentrated ball of acid in his hands and throws it at the chosen location. It bursts into acrid vapor that fills the area. The vapor quickly thickens, restricting vision and movement (-3 to THAC0, -30% movement speed). Each round, creatures in the cloud suffer 3d6 points of acid damage and must save vs. poison to avoid intoxication. An intoxicated creature loses 2 points of Strength and Dexterity for 1 round and must make another save or suffer severe poisoning: 2 points of damage per second during the current round and 1 point per second during the following round.~

@769 = ~Physical Image~
@7610 = ~Physical Image (Illusion)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 1 round / level
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell creates an illusory duplicate of the mage. Blurring and spatial distortion make it difficult to distinguish the image from its creator. Each attack against the mage has a 50% chance of striking the image instead.
Unlike the level 2 spell Mirror Image, this duplicate does not disappear when struck. Only dispelling, magical divination or the end of the spell removes it.
With experience, the mage can create 1D2 images at level 17 and 1D2 +1 copies at level 22.
This spell cannot be active at the same time as Mirror Image.~
@76101 = ~Physical Image (Illusion)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell creates two or three illusory images of the mage. The replicas move exactly as he does. Blurring and spatial distortion make them difficult to distinguish from their creator. As a result of this, every time the mage is attacked, there is a 66% chance (two images) or 75% (three images) that the attack strikes an image instead, leaving him unharmed.
Unlike the level 2 spell Mirror Image, these images do not disappear when struck. Only dispelling, magical divination or the end of the spell removes them.
This spell cannot be active at the same time as Mirror Image.~
@76102 = ~Physical Image (Illusion)
Level: 6
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell creates two or three illusory images of the recipient. The replicas move exactly as he does. Blurring and spatial distortion make them difficult to distinguish from their creator. As a result of this, every time the recipient is attacked, there is a 66% chance (two images) or 75% (three images) that the attack strikes an image instead, leaving him unharmed.
Unlike the level 2 spell Mirror Image, these images do not disappear when struck. Only dispelling, magical divination or the end of the spell removes them.
The warlord's experience allows him to create an extra image at level 22.
This spell cannot be active at the same time as Mirror Image.~
@761021 = ~Physical Image (Illusion)
Level: 6
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell creates two or three illusory images of the recipient. The replicas move exactly as he does. Blurring and spatial distortion make them difficult to distinguish from their creator. As a result of this, every time the recipient is attacked, there is a 66% chance (two images) or 75% (three images) that the attack strikes an image instead, leaving him unharmed.
Unlike the level 2 spell Mirror Image, these images do not disappear when struck. Only dispelling, magical divination or the end of the spell removes them.
The warlord's experience allows him to create an extra image at level 22.
This spell cannot be active at the same time as Mirror Image.

All allies within 5 meters of the target also benefit from reduced effects of the spell: they are protected by a replica for 13 rounds.~

@7611 = ~Giant's Strength~
@7612 = ~Giant's Strength (Alteration)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 5 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell significantly increases the physical strength of the warlord, granting him the strength of a giant. The strength obtained through this spell is determined by a die roll, modified by the level of the caster, according to the following table:

Level 12 to 14: 1D4
Level 15 to 17: 1D6
Level 18+     : 1D4 +2

The die result determines the strength granted to the wizard:
1: 19 strength (Hill Giant)
2: 20 strength (Stone Giant)
3: 21 strength (Frost Giant)
4: 22 strength (Fire Giant)
5: 23 strength (Cloud Giant)
6: 24 strength (Storm Giant)~
@76121 = ~Giant's Strength (Alteration)
Level: 6
Range: 0
Duration: 25 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This spell significantly increases the physical strength of the warlord, granting him the strength of a giant. A d4 roll determines the strength granted to the wizard, according to the following table:
1: 21 strength (Frost Giant)
2: 22 strength (Fire Giant)
3: 23 strength (Cloud Giant)
4: 24 strength (Storm Giant)~
