@7613 = ~Static Discharge~
@7614 = ~Static Discharge (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: 30 meters
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: half

Based on the spell "Static Shock", this spell is an improvement that allows you to concentrate the area's static electricity on a single creature. The result is a dazzling lightning bolt that strikes it, inflicting 1D6 points of damage per caster level (max 20D6). A save vs. spell reduces by half the damage received.~
@76141 = ~Static Discharge (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: 30 meters
Duration: instantaneous
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: half

Based on the spell "Static Shock", this spell is an improvement that allows you to concentrate the area's static electricity on a single creature. The result is a dazzling lightning bolt that strikes it, inflicting 20D6 points of damage. A save vs. spell reduces by half the damage received.~

@7615 = ~Phantom Hit~
@7616 = ~Phantom Hit (Evocation)
Level: 6
Range: 15 meters
Duration: instantaneous/special
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

Like "Ghost Hit", this spell conjures from nothing a sword of pure magic that inevitably hits the designated target. The similarity ends there. The blow delivered by Phantom Hit is far more precise and devastating.
The victim suffers an initial hit inflicting 3D8 points of damage. Then it will suffer one of the following random effects:
- 3D8 points of magic damage
- 5D8 points of fire damage, 35% chance of major damage and burning in case of a failed save vs. spell.
- 6D8 points of cold damage, 40% chance of major damage and freezing in case of a failed save vs. spell.
- 8D8 points of electricity damage, 50% chance of major damage and incapacitating internal trauma in case of a failed save vs. spell.
- 8D8 points of slashing damage, 50% chance of major damage and decapitation in case of a failed save vs. death.
- 10D8 points of acid damage, 60% chance of major damage and complete dissolution in case of a failed save vs. death.

In the case of major damage, D8 are counted as D6 +2. All saving throws against this spell are made at -4.~
